        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "040ae3df-a2d0-5186-b8fb-f67992c5c1ea",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim Rice, Leslie Marmon Silko, Elton John, Kenneth Lincoln\n- Works: \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight\", The Lion King, Ceremony\n- Organizations: Disney, Penguin\n- Topics: awards, Native American Renaissance\n\nFacts:\n- Tim Rice was born on 10 November 1944 and is an English author and lyricist.\n- Leslie Marmon Silko was born on March 5, 1948, was born Leslie Marmon, and is a Laguna Pueblo writer.\n- Ceremony is a novel by Leslie Marmon Silko that was first published by Penguin in March 1977.\n- \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight\" is a song from Disney's 1994 animated film The Lion King.\n- Elton John composed \"Can You Feel the Love Tonight,\" and Tim Rice wrote its lyrics.\n- Tim Rice has won Academy, Golden Globe, Tony, and Grammy awards.\n- Leslie Marmon Silko is one of the key figures in the First Wave of the Native American Renaissance, a term used by literary critic Kenneth Lincoln.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
